---
title: Lemongrass Beef Banh Mi
servings: 2
course: lunch
cuisine: Vietnamese
image: https://img.youtube.com/vi/oU9ct7GKEgs/maxresdefault.jpg
tags: beef, bread, quick
source: https://youtu.be/oU9ct7GKEgs
---

Peel @carrot{1} and grate it into matchsticks with a #julienne peeler{}. Season generously with @salt{1%pinch}, mix by hand, and let sit for ~{5%minutes} to draw out water.

In a #saucepan{}, combine @sugar{50%g}, @rice vinegar{50%ml}, and @water{50%ml}. Heat gently just until the sugar dissolves completely; do not boil.

Slice @cucumber{0.5} in half lengthwise, cut into long batons, and remove the watery seeds so the sandwich won't get soggy.

Squeeze the purged grated carrots firmly between your hands to extract excess moisture, then place them into a clean #jar{}. Pour the warm brine over the carrots. Add @garlic{1%clove} and @red chili{1} (or coriander seeds/peppercorns if desired), seal the jar, and set aside.

Thinly slice tender @beef{250%g} (such as sirloin, flank, or rump steak) into fine strips.

Finely mince @garlic{2%cloves} and @lemongrass{1%stalk}.

In a #dish{}, combine the beef with @sugar{1%tsp}, @oyster sauce{1%tbsp}, @light soy sauce{1%tbsp}, @dark soy sauce{0.5%tsp}, minced garlic, and minced lemongrass. Mix thoroughly with your hands to coat every piece. Let marinate for at least ~{10%minutes} (or overnight).

In a #blender cup{}, add @egg{1}, @dijon mustard{1%tsp}, a pinch of @&salt{1%pinch}, a squeeze of @lime juice{1%tsp}, and @sunflower oil{150%ml}. Insert an #immersion blender{} all the way to the bottom, start blending, and slowly move it up and down until a thick, smooth mayonnaise forms.

Transfer a portion of mayonnaise to a #small bowl{} and stir in @sriracha sauce{1%tbsp} to taste (or customize with garlic, soy sauce, and sesame oil).

Heat a #skillet{} with @vegetable oil{1%tbsp} over high heat. Add the marinated beef and sear quickly for ~{2-3%minutes}, keeping it tender and juicy.

Cut a soft, lightly baked @baguette{1} into portions and slice open lengthwise. Generously spread the mayonnaise onto both inner sides of the bread.

Layer the cooked lemongrass beef inside, followed by the cucumber batons, a generous handful of drained pickled carrots, and fresh @coriander{1%bunch} (leaves and tender stems). Finish with a few drops of @maggi liquid seasoning{0.5%tsp} and serve immediately.
